<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44671" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏlon</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏlo</span></b>  (the latter in <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 2, 1,
			2</span></i>), ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σόλων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A famous legislator of the Athenians</i>, <i>one of the seven sages of Greece</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 7,
				27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de
				Or. 1, 44, 197</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Leg.
				2, 23, 59</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 25, 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 3, 31
					<i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 10,
				274</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aerumnosi Solones,</span>”
				i. e. <i>philosophers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers. 3, 79 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A commander in Pydna</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 44,
			45</span></i>.</div>
